{"path":"experimental/memory_resource/do_is_equal","title":"std::experimental::pmr::memory_resource::do_is_equal","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::pmr::memory_resource::</span>do_is_equal","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/memory_resource/do_is_equal","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"Compares *this for equality with other.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-libfund_ts\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">virtual</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> is_equal<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> memory_resource<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> other <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-libfund-ts t-mark-ts\">(library fundamentals TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Compares <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> for equality with <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code>.\n</p><p>Two <code>memory_resource</code>s compare equal if and only if memory allocated from one <code>memory_resource</code> can be deallocated from the other and vice versa.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The most-derived type of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> may not match the most derived type of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code>. A derived class implementation therefore must typically check whether the most derived types of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> match using <span class=\"t-lc\">dynamic_cast</span>, and immediately return <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code> if the cast fails.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/memory_resource/is_equal\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>is_equal</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  compare for equality with another <code>memory_resource</code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/memory_resource","title":"std::experimental::pmr::memory_resource"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::pmr::memory_resource::do_is_equal","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Compares *this for equality with other."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The most-derived type of other may not match the most derived type of *this."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"is_equal","note":"compare for equality with another memory_resource"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":97,"codeBlockCount":0}
